          "text": "24",
          "correct": true
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "30",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut: Trailing zeroes in <span class=\"math\">n!</span> = Sum of quotients of <span class=\"math\">n</span> divided by powers of 5. <span class=\"math\">\\lfloor 100/5 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 100/25 \\rfloor + \\lfloor 100/125 \\rfloor = 20 + 4 + 0 = 24</span>. Full Solution: A trailing zero is produced by a factor of 10 = 2 × 5. In factorials, factors of 2 are more frequent than 5, so we count factors of 5. Multiples of 5 up to 100: <span class=\"math\">\\lfloor 100/5 \\rfloor = 20</span>. Multiples of 25 (extra factor of 5): <span class=\"math\">\\lfloor 100/25 \\rfloor = 4</span>. Multiples of 125: <span class=\"math\">\\lfloor 100/125 \\rfloor = 0</span>. Total factors of 5 = <span class=\"math\">20 + 4 = 24</span>. Hence, 24 trailing zeroes.",
