        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "0",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "2",
          "correct": false
        }
      ],
      "solution": "Shortcut: Subtract the two equations to eliminate x²: (a-b)x + (b-a) = 0 ⇒ (a-b)(x-1)=0. Since a ≠ b, the common root x = 1. Substitute x=1 in first equation: 1 + a + b = 0 ⇒ a + b = -1. Full Solution: Let α be the common root. Then α² + aα + b = 0 and α² + bα + a = 0. Subtracting gives (a-b)α + (b-a) = 0 ⇒ (a-b)(α-1)=0. As a ≠ b, α = 1. Putting α=1 in α² + aα + b = 0 gives 1 + a + b = 0 ⇒ a + b = -1.",
